WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.570
-Welcome back, everybody. I'm
here with Lin-Manuel Miranda!

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.939
Now, his --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.341
Let's talk about
"In The Heights."

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.176
This is the movie adaptation

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.545
of your Tony-winning
Broadway musical.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.847
You started writing this
when you were in college.

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.982
You were 19
when you were writing this.

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:18.551
And what did you envision

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.986
when you were --
when you were writing this?

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.388
-Yeah, I was not much older than
"The King of Wishful Thinking"

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.323
-Exactly.
-...that you saw.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:25.725
But I -- I honestly --

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:29.095
I just -- I knew I wanted
a life in musicals.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:32.831
I directed "West Side Story"
my senior year of high school,

00:00:32.831 --> 00:00:35.768
and I knew that was kind of it
for Puerto Rican guys

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.770
in musical theater.
That's all that existed.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.038
-Yeah.
-I love that show.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.472
-That's interesting.
-But it was a long time ago.

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:43.909
And -- And I just kind of
was writing what was missing.

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:45.277
And I wanted to, you know,

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:47.914
I wanted to write musicals
starring Latinos,

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.515
telling different stories and --

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.083
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.286
Like, and here we are
20 years later, right?

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.920
And now I'm on "The Tonight
Show" talking to you.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.988
Like, that's crazy!

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:57.657
-[ Laughing ] Yeah, that's --

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.259
It shows how much work
goes into all of this stuff.

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:01.627
-Yeah.
-Lightning in a --

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:03.996
I mean, come on.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.932
-And don't stop.
And you never stopped.

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.667
And you just go, "We're just
gonna keep doing this.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:09.936
I'm going to write this."

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.371
And it is brilliantly done.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:14.674
The choreography, the singing.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:15.975
Anthony Ramos.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.643
-What a superstar.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.613
Superstar!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.348
-It's just -- It's colorful.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:26.052
It moves. It's hopeful.
It's a beautiful story.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.553
And, yeah, it just gives you

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.021
everything you want to see
in a movie.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:30.289
I loved it. I needed it.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:31.724
Like, I need a film --

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.661
I love "Godzilla vs. Kong."
That's all good.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.763
I need this, though. I needed
this. And I was like, "Oh."

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.332
And then, there's a scene
where it's like,

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.401
"Oof, this is going to get sad.
You're not going to do it."

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.502
And yeah, it does.
It gets you, and you go, "Oh."

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:44.871
It's so great.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.841
But I just -- I freaked out.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:51.978
But when I talked to you, when
Jon was doing the movie, you go,

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:55.548
"Yeah, and I think I might -- I
might do something in the movie.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.550
You were not going to be in it.
-I was not going to be in it.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.252
I was -- I was never
planning to be in it.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.620
I had my Broadway experience,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.123
which was a miraculous
experience.

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:07.192
I went from substitute teacher
to Broadway composer.

00:02:07.192 --> 00:02:10.630
I will never make a leap
that big again in my life.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.231
And, so, I was very content

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.366
to let Anthony Ramos
and this incredible cast

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:16.469
kind of have
their own experience.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.905
And Quiara, my co-writer, and
Jon Chu, kept dropping hints,

00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:22.241
like, "We haven't cast
Piragua Guy yet.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:24.010
We haven't cast Piragua Guy
yet."

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.411
And I was like, "That's cool.
That's cool."

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.681
And then Quiara
said two things --

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:31.251
She wrote the screenplay,
and she's a genius.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:36.389
But she also said, "I think that
we might have to cut Piragua,

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.958
because it doesn't really
move the plot along.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.094
But I thought of a way
not to cut it."

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.730
And I went, "What is the way?
I love that song."

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.965
And she said,
"If you play Piragua Guy,

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.500
they won't cut Piragua Guy."
-You can't cut Piragua Guy!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.802
-Yeah.
-He's my favorite.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.404
Dude, the song is so good.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.872
-Yeah.
-It pays off.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.475
-Yeah. And she also said, like,
"If you hadn't written this,

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.776
you'd be begging
to be in this movie.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.344
This is what
you always dreamed of."

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.979
And, like, that kind of
got through to me.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.615
And I'm so glad I was a part
of it, because it's just --

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.516
I'm so proud of what Jon made.

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:07.186
And there's a moment
where I sing with Anthony,

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:10.022
and he played my old part,
and I get to duet with him.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.725
And I'm on a fire escape,
and he's a floor below me,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.728
and I'm singing a new harmony,
and he's singing my old harmony.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.964
And there's all these,
like, full-circle moments.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.832
It was really --
It was like a dream come true.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.302
Every day was a dream come true.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.771
-It's so well written.
It's so good.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.639
And you go, yeah,
at the end, you're clapping,

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.374
even though I was
watching at home,

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.642
and I was just, like, clapping
by -- I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:03:30.642 --> 00:03:32.011
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.580
Here's Lin-Manuel Miranda
in "In The Heights."

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.748
Take a look.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:36.782
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:39.318
[ Singing in Spanish ]

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:45.925 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:52.531 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:55.234
-[ Singing in Spanish ]

00:03:55.234 --> 00:04:03.309 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:11.417 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:19.492 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.894
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.996
-It's that --
It's how you feel it.

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:25.664
It's so well done.

00:04:25.664 --> 00:04:29.001
I also want to say, the --

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.036
Tomorrow night, it opens
the Tribeca Film Festival,

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.039
which means a lot
to New York City,

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.241
but also to everyone
in the business,

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.543
I mean, what they've done
with that festival.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.745
But you're opening
the film festival.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:41.413
You're going to be
in Washington Heights

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:42.682
showing this to a theater.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:45.985
-We premiere this movie
on 175th Street, y'all.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.020
Like, it's in
Washington Heights.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.255
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.923
-The best --

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.659
That -- Talk about emotional.
That's like --

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.928
It is a love letter
to Washington Heights, really,

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.396
and New York City.

00:04:57.396 --> 00:05:00.332
And I think that's going
to be another special moment.

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.001
-It's going to be insane.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.569
-Buddy, I love you so much.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:04.804
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.705
We love you. Lin-Manuel Miranda.

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:10.209
"In The Heights" is in theaters
and on HBO Max this Thursday.

